      "function": {
        "description": "Read, list, or kill Bash commands still running in this Cake run. Sessions do not survive Cake exit or resume.\n\nUse `read` with a Bash session ID to receive only output produced since the previous call. It returns when output arrives, the command exits, or the optional `wait` window ends. `wait` takes whole seconds, defaults to 10 seconds, is capped at 120 seconds, and `0` polls immediately. A completed session remains available briefly; repeated reads return its final output and exit status.\n\nUse `kill` to terminate the session's entire process group. Use `list` to find live and recently exited sessions. Unknown session IDs return an error naming active sessions.\n",
        "name": "BashSession",
