      "function": {
        "description": "Edit text in files using literal search-and-replace. All non-no-op edits in a single call succeed atomically or none are applied. Edits with identical old_text and new_text are skipped.\n\nThe configured `edit_max_file_bytes` limit caps the input file size Edit will read (16 MiB by default); a larger file is rejected before reading, and `\"unlimited\"` disables the cap. This limit is independent of `read_max_output_bytes`, which bounds Read output.\n\nGuidance:\n- Always Read the file first before editing.\n- old_text must match exactly once in the file. Include 3+ surrounding lines for uniqueness.\n- For multi-line matches, preserve exact whitespace and indentation.\n- Special characters in JSON (backticks, quotes, backslashes) must be escaped.\n- Each successful edit invalidates any earlier read of that file. Re-read before editing the same file again.\n- The parameters are named old_text and new_text (not old_string/new_string).\n",
        "name": "Edit",
        "parameters": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "edits": {
              "description": "The edits to make to the file. Edits with identical old_text and new_text are no-ops; they are skipped and reported without changing the file. The max number of edits you can do at once is 20.",
